				)
			)
			(property "Description" "One-cell Li-ion protection IC, SOT-23-6 | DW01A | LCSC C351410 (PUOLOP). Overcharge 4.30 V +/-50 mV, release 4.10 V; over-discharge 2.40 V, release 3.00 V; overcurrent 150 mV +/-30 mV across the external FET stack (delay 7 ms typ), short-circuit 1.36 V typ but specified 0.82-1.75 V min-max (delay 400 us); Iq 3 uA. CAUTION: at the 1.75 V corner the fast short-circuit path does not fire with any realistic cell + 3-FET stack, because the stack only develops ~0.6-1.4 V into a dead short - a short is instead caught by the 150 mV overcurrent path at 7 ms. Vendor spreads matter: the Slkor DW01A is 4.3 V +/-50 mV (+/-80 mV over temperature) overcharge with 0.15 V +/-20 mV overcurrent, while other DW01A datasheets specify 4.25 V and +/-30 mV - PIN THE VENDOR AT ORDER TIME, since the 4.22 V low corner sits under the BQ21040's 4.23 V regulation maximum. Drives LOW-SIDE N-FETs only (no charge pump), so it sits in the battery NEGATIVE path: VCC via 1k+100nF to cell +, GND to cell - (B-), VM to board GND (P-) via 2k, OD/OC to the two gates. Replaces MAX17303G+ on the base station together with 3x FS8205A (Q1/Q2/Q3, ~21.0 mOhm stack). Pin 2 is named VM here; some DW01 datasheets label the same pin CS. Pinout from the LCSC/EasyEDA library for C351410, corroborated by the DW01A datasheet."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
					(justify left bottom)
				)
			)
