				)
			)
			(property "Description" "Dual N-channel MOSFET, common drain, SOT-23-6 | FS8205A | LCSC C2830320 (TECH PUBLIC). 20 V, 6 A, Rds(on) 31.5 mOhm/FET @ Vgs 2.5 V and 25 mOhm max @ 4.5 V. Back-to-back pair for 1-cell battery protection with a DW01A. PINS 2 AND 5 ARE THE SAME INTERNAL DRAIN NODE - solder BOTH to the drain net for current capacity. Base station fits THREE of these in parallel (Q1/Q2/Q3). The DW01A senses its 150 mV +/-30 mV overcurrent threshold across the WHOLE stack, so the trip point IS the FET stack resistance: 21.0 mOhm with three packages gives ~7.1 A typ / ~5.7 A min at 25 C and ~4.1 A at the hot corner (Rds +40 percent), against ~2.7 A hot-min with only two. Three is the sweet spot - a fourth would push the cold-typ trip to ~9.5 A, at or past an 18650's continuous rating, so it would stop protecting the cell. NOTE the trip rises with cell voltage (more gate drive) and falls as the FETs heat. Pinout from the LCSC/EasyEDA library for C2830320."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
